    <circle cx="150" cy="95" r="18" fill="var(--bronze)" opacity=".22"/>
  </svg>
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="sys-id"><span class="dot"></span>IAP / 01 — Private invitation</p>
    <div class="hero-mark">
      <span class="iap-big">IAP</span>
      <span class="iap-sub">Independent ArtiBytte Partners</span>
    </div>
    <h1>Partner with us, product by product.</h1>
    <p class="lede"><strong style="color:#f0ede6;font-weight:600">This isn't a job offer.</strong> It's how ArtiBytte works with outside specialists — one product, one written agreement, no full-time seat.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pad reveal" id="story">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="story">
      <div class="body">
        <p>ArtiBytte is a founder-led studio, kept small on purpose, building one family of products — ArtiPlay, ArtiStock, ArtiSnack, ArtiField, VEX AI. IAP is how everything outside that core team gets built.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull">
        <p>A partner network that collaborates with ArtiBytte through clearly defined commercial agreements.</p>
        <span>How we think about IAP internally</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pillars">
      <div class="pillar">
        <span class="pillar-num">i.</span>
        <h4>Defined work</h4>
        <p>Scope and deliverables set before anything starts — never figured out along the way.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <span class="pillar-num">ii.</span>
        <h4>Shared standards</h4>
        <p>One design system, one code standard, across every product a partner touches.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <span class="pillar-num">iii.</span>
        <h4>Commercial clarity</h4>
        <p>How you're paid is written down, agreed, and never assumed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pad light reveal" id="tracks" aria-labelledby="tracks-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="tracks-heading">Where partners plug in.</h2>
      <p>Most engagements fall into one of three tracks.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="iap-tracks">
      <div class="iap-track">
        <span class="idx">i.</span>
        <h3>Engineering</h3>
        <p>Web, mobile, backend, AI integration and security work on a defined module or product — scoped, reviewed, and shipped alongside the core team's standards.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="iap-track">
        <span class="idx">ii.</span>
        <h3>Design</h3>
        <p>UI/UX, brand and motion work for a specific product surface, following the shared ArtiBytte design system rather than starting from a blank page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="iap-track">
        <span class="idx">iii.</span>
        <h3>Business &amp; specialist</h3>
        <p>QA, documentation, domain consulting, or go-to-market support for a launch — sized to the actual scope of the work.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pad reveal" id="tiers" aria-labelledby="tiers-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="section-tag"><span class="dot"></span>IAP / 02 — Hierarchy</p>
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="tiers-heading">The IAP hierarchy.</h2>
      <p>One core progression, four steps deep. Every partner enters as a Specialist and can move up as far as the relationship goes — or stay exactly where it is, on purpose. Category, engagement and process are each set individually within whichever tier applies.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tier-path">
      <div class="tier-node">
        <div class="tier-node-rail">
          <div class="tier-node-circle">1</div>
          <div class="tier-node-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-node-body">
          <span class="tier-label">IAP-1</span>
          <h3>Specialist</h3>
          <p>Engaged for one specific task or a short-term project — the entry point for almost every new partner.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-node">
        <div class="tier-node-rail">
          <div class="tier-node-circle">2</div>
          <div class="tier-node-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-node-body">
          <span class="tier-label">IAP-2</span>
          <h3>Certified Partner</h3>
          <p>Vetted through delivered work and trusted with recurring engagements across more than one product.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-node">
        <div class="tier-node-rail">
          <div class="tier-node-circle">3</div>
          <div class="tier-node-line"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-node-body">
          <span class="tier-label">IAP-3</span>
          <h3>Lead Partner</h3>
          <p>Leads an independent product or module team, coordinating other specialists working on that build.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-node">
        <div class="tier-node-rail">
          <div class="tier-node-circle">4</div>
        </div>
        <div class="tier-node-body">
          <span class="tier-label">IAP-4</span>
          <h3>Strategic Partner</h3>
          <p>A long-term relationship with a deeper commercial and IP arrangement, tied closely to a product's ongoing success.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="tier-branch-label">A separate path — not a step up</p>
    <div class="tier-x-card">
      <div class="tier-node-circle">X</div>
      <div>
        <h3>IAP-X — Expert Network</h3>
        <p>Not a step to climb toward — a standing pool we call on for a one-off, specific need. No application path, no promotion into it, no ongoing commitment either way.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pad reveal" id="categories" aria-labelledby="categories-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="section-tag"><span class="dot"></span>IAP / 03 — Category</p>
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="categories-heading">Category — your area of contribution.</h2>
      <p>Whatever tier a partner sits at, the work itself falls into one of four categories.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cat-grid">
      <div class="cat-cell">
        <span class="idx">a.</span>
        <h3>Engineering</h3>
        <p class="cat-desc">Where products get built.</p>
        <p class="cat-list">Web · Mobile · Backend · AI · Security · DevOps · Database</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-cell">
        <span class="idx">b.</span>
        <h3>Product</h3>
        <p class="cat-desc">Where scope and quality stay honest.</p>
        <p class="cat-list">Product management · Business analysis · QA · Technical writing</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-cell">
        <span class="idx">c.</span>
        <h3>Design</h3>
        <p class="cat-desc">Where it looks and feels like ArtiBytte.</p>
        <p class="cat-list">UI/UX · Brand · Motion · Graphics</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cat-cell">
        <span class="idx">d.</span>
        <h3>Business</h3>
        <p class="cat-desc">Where products reach the people who'll use them.</p>
        <p class="cat-list">Sales · Marketing · Customer success · Consulting</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cat-link">Category runs independent of tier — <em>every tier, IAP-1 through IAP-4, draws from all four.</em></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pad light reveal" id="comp" aria-labelledby="comp-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="section-tag"><span class="dot"></span>IAP / 04 — Engagement</p>
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="comp-heading">Engagement — the commercial arrangement.</h2>
      <p>There's no single formula. The arrangement is matched to the tier and the scope of work, and set out in writing before anything begins — discussed and agreed with you directly, not assumed.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="comp-guarantee">
      <span class="check">✓</span>
      <p><strong>Commercial clarity, in practice:</strong> every arrangement below is discussed, defined, and agreed in writing before any work begins — never assumed, never retroactive.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="comp-row">
      <p class="comp-section-label">Paid for the work</p>
      <div class="comp-pair">
        <div class="comp-cell-v2 comp-cell-work">
          <span class="letter">a.</span>
          <h4>Project fee</h4>
          <p>The straightforward model: a fixed amount for clearly scoped, well-defined work. One agreed price for one agreed deliverable — the default for a single module or feature.</p>
          <span class="best-when">Best when the task is small and predictable.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comp-cell-v2 comp-cell-work">
          <span class="letter">b.</span>
          <h4>Milestones</h4>
          <p>The staged-delivery model: the same fixed-price logic, broken into agreed checkpoints. Payment released as each stage ships — built for larger or longer-running work.</p>
          <span class="best-when">Best when the upfront budget is uncertain — sometimes paired with a revenue share.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="comp-row">
      <p class="comp-section-label">Paid on the outcome</p>
      <div class="comp-pair">
        <div class="comp-cell-v2 comp-cell-outcome">
          <span class="letter">c.</span>
          <h4>Revenue share or royalty</h4>
          <p>Tied directly to a specific product's ongoing success rather than the hours put in — both sides share the upside. Every term (gross vs. net, duration, scope) is spelled out in writing, product by product, before work starts.</p>
          <span class="written-cue">
            <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8"><path d="M12 19l7-7 3 3-7 7-3-3z"/><path d="M18 13l-1.5-7.5L2 2l3.5 14.5L13 18l5-5z"/><path d="M2 2l7.586 7.586"/><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="2"/></svg>
            Terms fixed in writing per product
          </span>
          <span class="best-when">Best for a contributor who builds something reusable, not a one-off task.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="comp-cell-v2 comp-cell-outcome comp-cell-strategic">
          <span class="letter">d.</span>
          <h4>Product-specific equity</h4>
          <p>The deepest link to outcome: a stake in one product's future. Reserved for long-term contributors actually shaping where that product goes.</p>
          <span class="best-when">Best for a genuinely strategic, long-term role — not ordinary project work.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="comp-note">Any revenue share or royalty is defined precisely in writing before work begins — gross vs. net, before or after refunds, chargebacks, taxes and payment-processing fees, the term length, and whether it applies to one product or the company as a whole.</p>

    <p class="comp-note" style="margin-top:6px">Not all company equity is on the table for a single module. The more logical default is a <strong>product-specific</strong> revenue share or royalty — for example, a developer on Cygnus 658 earning a defined 5% of net receipts for 24 months, while ArtiBytte ownership itself stays with its founders and shareholders. Exact percentages and terms are negotiated and documented per case.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="pad light reveal" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="section-tag"><span class="dot"></span>IAP / 05 — Process</p>
    <div class="head">
      <h2 id="how-heading">Process — how collaboration happens.</h2>
      <p>From this conversation to shipped work, at any tier.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="iap-steps">
      <div class="iap-step"><div class="num">01</div><div><h4>We talk.</h4><p>You reply to the email that brought you here, and we figure out where your skills line up with something we're building.</p></div></div>
      <div class="iap-step"><div class="num">02</div><div><h4>Scope it, in writing.</h4><p>Defined work, defined pay — written and agreed before you start, not after.</p></div></div>
      <div class="iap-step"><div class="num">03</div><div><h4>Build it, the ArtiBytte way.</h4><p>Shared standards, not a blank page — one design system, one code bar, across every product in the family.</p></div></div>
      <div class="iap-step"><div class="num">04</div><div><h4>Deliver, get paid, stay in the network.</h4><p>Strong engagements lead to more work — and occasionally, a seat on the core team.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

