    <p class="comp-note" style="margin-top:14px">This is the real multiplier: a new product doesn't start from zero — it starts from everything the last one already solved.</p>

    <div class="ceiling-block">
      <p class="cb-label">But there's a ceiling</p>
      <p>If one person has to approve every change, every hire, every payment, every release — that's not a system, it's a bottleneck. So the core doesn't just build products; it owns the standards a partner works inside of:</p>
      <div class="ceiling-list">
        <span>Standardized contracts</span>
        <span>Git workflow</span>
        <span>Coding standards</span>
        <span>Security access</span>
        <span>QA gates</span>
        <span>Documentation</span>
        <span>Payment rules</span>
      </div>
    </div>

